Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:25:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] CF-CLONE-2: a unit still deploying is cloned whatever it
 carries; a clone its registration visit ends takes no move apart

Two Clone refusals are removed:

- "is cloned with a deploy countdown and carries riders / as a carrier's rider" and "... and its clone's row spawns an
  area object or a push as it deploys". The creator's order (countdown setter before the setup, after it for a
  carrier) and the setter's entry into the deploying state now run as they are: a carrier's clone never enters the
  deploying state and makes no riders, and its riders' clones take their riders' countdowns; any other clone enters
  the deploying state through its setter, so a Mega Knight's clone pushes again. Not traced from the client and held
  by no recording (b): it follows crforge's own creator and setter.
- "moves apart from its clone without its movement component": a character its registration visit has ended takes no
  move apart. The kamikaze Goblin Demolisher's clone, cut to 1 hit point after its lifetime drain step was set from
  its full maximum, loses that 1 at its first hit points' visit and dies before its move apart; its original moves
  apart alone. A living character without its movement component is still refused.

BattleCloneTest: the deploying carrier's refusal test becomes the carrier cloned with its riders; a Mega Knight
cloned as it deploys, its clone pushing; the kamikaze Goblin Demolisher's clone dying with no move apart.
