@@ -2486,6 +2486,10 @@ These are supplied answers, recorded on the classes that carry them and listed h
 
   A unit still deploying as the Clone reaches it is cloned with its countdown. The countdown setter puts the clone into the deploying state with the unit's countdown, and the clone then leaves it for state 8 with the countdown kept. The unit goes to 8 with its own.
 
+  The clone's entry into the deploying state is its setter's, so a row whose entry spawns an area object or a push spawns it again from the clone: a Mega Knight cloned as it deploys pushes the enemies around its clone. A carrier's clone is set up before its countdown, so it never enters the deploying state and makes no riders; its riders still deploying are cloned with their own countdowns and attached to it. Neither is traced from the client or held by a recording: both follow the creator's order and the setter's entry as crforge has them (CF-CLONE-2).
+
+  A clone that its registration visit ends takes no move apart. A row with a lifetime drains its hit points from a step set from its maximum as it is made, so its clone, cut to 1 of 1 after, loses that 1 at its first hit points' visit: the Goblin Demolisher's kamikaze form cloned dies at once, before any move apart, and its original moves apart alone.
+
   In 8 both countdowns run down 50 a visit with no resume at 0. A move apart that reaches its ten visits while its unit's countdown still runs sets NO_MOVE on itself, which the unit carries while the run is listed, holding it still, and asks again each visit. Once the countdown has ended it resumes the unit and finishes.
 
   The burst clock of a unit that walks in bursts steps by half the buff-scaled 100 a visit, so under the Clone buff's speed of -100 it stands still.
@@ -2494,8 +2498,6 @@ These are supplied answers, recorded on the classes that carry them and listed h
 
